# Note: packages/fixtures/data/ IS tracked.
#
# The parser tests read recorded PSX responses and never touch the network, so
# the fixtures are test inputs, not build output. They must be versioned or a
# fresh clone has no working test suite.
#
# They are protected from publication by `"private": true` on the fixtures
# package, not by .gitignore. Do not add them here.

# Reference Python libraries, removed after their useful content was extracted
# into packages/client/src and docs/indicators-spec.md.
#
# Two of the three were unlicensed or proprietary, and one shipped a GitHub
# Actions workflow that exfiltrated a PyPI token to a hardcoded IP on every
# push. Keeping third-party source in-tree was a liability with no remaining
# benefit. See docs/indicators-spec.md for what was taken.
ref/
